window.docContents[239].resolve({"/Ideals-and-splitting/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Ideals-and-splitting":{"contents":"\n\nFor primes  dividing , the ideals  and\n in Zsqrtd d have coordinate membership criteria.\n\nThose concrete ideals have quotient descriptions by ,\nwhich supply the primality proofs.\n\nThe quotient descriptions prove that both ideals are prime in the relevant\nconcrete splitting branch.\n\nThe stable splitting API packages split, inert, and ramified behavior for primes\nin quadratic number fields.\n\nFor odd primes not dividing the parameter, splitting and inertia are controlled\nby the Legendre symbol.\n\nThe prime  is handled by the expected congruences modulo  and modulo\n.\n\nThe  examples verify ideal factorizations above \nand , serving as concrete tests of the ideal API.\n\nA future cleanup should unify the odd-prime and two-adic splitting statements\nusing a Kronecker-symbol formulation where that abstraction is helpful.\n\n","context":"Quadratic Number Fields Blueprint","header":"5. Ideals and splitting","id":"/Ideals-and-splitting/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Ideals-and-splitting"}});